  "claims": [
    {
      "id": "clm:5e6638c9e1ab346a9e37430064722eb6b1e381cdd27b97170cd4be9a8d4ba96d",
      "text": "MongoDB advises against fixed thresholds below 100 ms; a OneUptime tutorial instead illustrates 50 ms after disabling management, so its example should not be treated as MongoDB recommended practice. (medium confidence) (verified as of 2026-03-31)",
      "source_url": "https://www.mongodb.com/docs/atlas/performance-advisor.md",
      "also": [
        "https://oneuptime.com/blog/post/2026-03-31-mongodb-how-to-use-mongodb-atlas-performance-advisor/view"
      ],
      "validation_status": "SUPPORTED",
      "evidence_ids": [
        "ev:97fca132518ea8311d7d3becc29ede7c8176d238cc6e7d1b6b8542c828a72b66",
        "ev:e8764f3e7945698789d317c7571bd5d0ee8133be4b58bf232e2cf699b36800a2"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "clm:478706367168ded5a77ed2f2f13328698d5b20f3e531a6c24365fae616a7a787",
      "text": "Atlas enables managed slow-operation thresholds by default on supported clusters and dynamically adjusts them using execution times across the cluster; 100 ms is the fixed fallback when management is disabled. (medium confidence) (verified as of 2026-10-14)",
      "source_url": "https://www.mongodb.com/docs/atlas/performance-advisor.md",
      "also": [
        "https://www.manning.com/preview/mongodb-in-action-third-edition/chapter-21",
        "https://github.com/awslabs/amazon-documentdb-tools/blob/master/compat-tool/README.md",
        "https://oneuptime.com/blog/post/2026-03-31-mongodb-atlas-query-profiler-cloud/view"
      ],
      "validation_status": "SUPPORTED",
      "evidence_ids": [
        "ev:e8764f3e7945698789d317c7571bd5d0ee8133be4b58bf232e2cf699b36800a2"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "clm:5954d3e9d61c7e8751e973ce293a9e3014bd41f4f9f87dcf1cf20ed50a432062",
      "text": "A 2022 support response says query frequency affects suggestions, so infrequent slow queries need not produce recommendations. (low confidence)",
      "source_url": "https://www.mongodb.com/community/forums/t/alert-all-the-time-query-targeting-scanned-objects-returned-has-gone-above-1000/168277",
      "also": [],
      "validation_status": "SUPPORTED",
      "evidence_ids": [
        "ev:6f8d432b9493184c90aff835b54e553699211418b2d8f4acea14ded85a91c6d1"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "clm:701b5edd668065ad7b3f7200321f2ad8b3707a5aa18087d1f3d95c33e94f95cc",
      "text": "MongoDB Atlas Query Insights templates read Performance Advisor slow logs and suggestions to report on query shapes; the template cannot create indexes. (low confidence) (verified as of 2026-10-30)",
      "source_url": "https://github.com/mongodb/agents",
      "also": [],
      "validation_status": "SUPPORTED",
      "evidence_ids": [
        "ev:3d4d2f8e37c757c9bf26f8b62d08a1220c313893986af722ee60565eb365f9ab"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "clm:63254a34c45d400965b848564345c1309f761b7782939cc28fed23f39595e8f3",
      "text": "Inference for safe index removal: absence of an Advisor suggestion cannot prove safety because recommendations depend on query frequency and captured slow-log evidence. (medium confidence)",
      "source_url": "https://www.mongodb.com/docs/atlas/performance-advisor.md",
      "also": [
        "https://www.mongodb.com/community/forums/t/alert-all-the-time-query-targeting-scanned-objects-returned-has-gone-above-1000/168277"
      ],
      "validation_status": "SUPPORTED",
      "evidence_ids": [
